=== TASK ===
# Signup Page

## Overview
Create a comprehensive, production-ready signup experience for LifeOps that supports standard email/password registration, social OAuth options, and optional rapid onboarding to select modules and connect initial integrations. The flow should be secure, accessible, and resilient, with proper session handling, 2FA readiness, and guards against incomplete or invalid data. This page is a gateway into the LifeOps ecosystem, tightly integrated with the existing authentication system and module/onboarding sub-flows, while remaining visually consistent with the project’s dark-mode design system.

## Page Description (Full Detail)
This page is the primary Registration flow for new users. Goals:
- Collect essential user information (email, name) and optional details (company).
- Provide password creation with a strength indicator.
- Offer terms acceptance with links to legal pages.
- Enable social signup (Google, GitHub) for faster onboarding.
- Present an optional quick onboarding panel to select modules (Projects, Content, Finance, Health) and optionally connect first integrations.
- On successful signup, route to onboarding/setup wizard or directly to the dashboard based on user choice.
- Validate input on client and server, provide real-time feedback, and handle edge cases (existing account, invalid email, weak password, terms not accepted).
- Persist user record, initiate email verification flow if required, and create an initial user session.
- Prepare for downstream onboarding flows: connect integrations, select modules, and guide the user to create their first cronjob/workflow.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, proper aria attributes, keyboard navigation, and high-contrast focus states.

Connected features and integrations:
- User Authentication: Email/password with optional OAuth (Google, GitHub), session management, and 2FA readiness (policy & UI hooks for enabling 2FA later).
- Onboarding / Setup Wizard (Linked post-signup): Optional quick onboarding selection of modules and initial integrations; data pre-populated to speed time-to-value.

UI elements and visuals (aligned with Visual Style):
- Inputs: Email, Full Name, Company (optional), Password with strength meter, Password visibility toggle.
- Password strength meter: dynamic, accessible indicator (weak/medium/strong) with color cues.
- Terms acceptance: Checkbox with inline links to Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, and Data Processing Addendum.
- Social signup: Icon buttons for Google and GitHub with accessible labels.
- Module selection: Inline, optional set of checkboxes or pill buttons for Projects, Content, Finance, Health; show summary of selected modules on the CTA region.
- Primary CTA: "Create account" or "Start onboarding" depending on the onboarding path.
- Secondary options: "Sign in" link for existing users, "Use quick onboarding" toggle (optional) to reveal module selection and integrations.
- Visual cues for errors: inline error messages, helper text, and an overall status banner if needed.

## Components to Build
- SignupPage
  - Subcomponents:
    - EmailInput: validates email format, shows inline helper text.
    - NameInput: validates non-empty.
    - CompanyInput (optional): simple text input.
    - PasswordInput: reveals strength meter, strength logic, and strength color coding.
    - TermsCheckbox: consent with accessible label and links.
    - SocialSignupRow: Google and GitHub buttons with icons; loading state and error handling.
    - ModuleSelector: multi-select pills or checkboxes for Projects, Content, Finance, Health; live summary.
    - OnboardingPreview: optional panel showing what onboarding will cover based on module selection.
    - OnboardingCTASection: primary CTA, secondary actions, and status indicators.
    - PasswordMeter: standalone meter component used by PasswordInput.
- EmailVerificationModal or PageFragment (if verification is needed before entry): handles sending/resenting verification tokens; shows status.
- ValidationMessages: shared component to render field-level errors and helper text.
- LoadingSpinner / ProgressDots: for network activity states.
- Toasts / Alerts: for success or error feedback (e.g., account exists, verification required).
- BackendAPIFacade (hook/service layer): encapsulates API calls for signup, OAuth, session initiation, and user profile creation.

## Implementation Requirements

### Frontend
- Frameworks: React (with TypeScript), preferably using a modern UI framework or custom components aligned to the design system.
- State management: useState and useReducer where appropriate; lift global session state to a shared AuthContext or similar pattern.
- Routing: integrate with the app’s router (e.g., React Router) to navigate to onboarding wizard or dashboard after signup.
- Accessibility: labels, aria-invalid, aria-live for errors, proper tab order, keyboard navigability.
- Runtime safety:
  - Initialize array states with correct types, e.g., useState<string[]>([]).
  - Guard against null/undefined results: use data ?? [] and Array.isArray(...) guards where mapping or filtering.
  - Validate API responses with Array.isArray checks and default to [] when needed.
- Validation:
  - Frontend validations for email pattern, password strength thresholds, required fields, and terms acceptance.
  - Debounce or throttle expensive validations if needed (e.g., availability checks).
- Security UI considerations:
  - Do not reveal password in plaintext; provide secure handling of tokens.
  - Do not log sensitive user data in client logs.
- Design system alignment:
  - Use the 12-column grid, consistent spacings (24–32px), dark-mode emphasis, and card-based sections.
  - Apply primary blue (#4F8CFF) for CTAs; secondary gray for secondary actions.
  - Implement hover/focus states as specified in the design guidelines.

### Backend
- Endpoints (draft, align with existing API conventions):
  - POST /auth/signup
    - Body: { email, name, password, company?, modules: string[], preferences?: object, onboardingPreferred?: boolean }
    - Effects: create user, hash password, create session, trigger email verification if needed, store onboarding module selections.
  - POST /auth/oauth/signup
    - Body: { provider: 'google'|'github', token: string, maybe profile? }
    - Effects: exchange token, create user if new, link OAuth to account, initiate 2FA readiness flow if applicable.
  - POST /auth/verify-email
    - Body: { token }
    - Effects: verify email, activate account, proceed to onboarding or dashboard.
  - GET /modules/availability (optional for server-side checks)
    - Return: available modules and defaults.
- Data models (adjust to existing schema):
  - User: id, email, name, company, passwordHash, createdAt, isEmailVerified, 2faEnabled, preferredModules[string[]], onboardingState, etc.
  - Session: sessionId, userId, createdAt, expiresAt, deviceInfo, ipAddress.
  - VerificationToken: userId, token, expiresAt, type ('email_verification').
  - OnboardingProgress: userId, modulesSelected[string[]], connectedIntegrations[string[]], lastUpdated.
- Security:
  - Enforce rate limiting on signup endpoints.
  - Enforce email verification flow before granting access to protected features, unless immediately entering onboarding.
  - Prepare 2FA integration hooks and flags to enable later (TOTP/backup codes).
  - Use parameterized queries and adhere to existing ORM patterns to prevent injection.
- Validation:
  - Server-side validation mirroring frontend checks.
  - Ensure null-safe data access: coalesce arrays, validate shapes with Array.isArray and defaults.
- Email verification:
  - Generate time-limited signed tokens; support token rotation and expiration handling.
- Logging & audit:
  - Audit trail for signup events, verification, onboarding actions, and failures.

### Integration
- Connect frontend signup flow with:
  - Authentication service for creating accounts and starting sessions.
  - Email service for verification tokens and emails.
  - Optional onboarding service for quick onboarding path (modules + integrations) post-signup.
- Data consistency:
  - Use schema-validated payloads; ensure all user-facing data is preserved across redirect to onboarding wizard.
- Error handling:
  - Map backend errors to user-friendly UI messages; prevent leakage of sensitive details.
  - Implement retry/backoff for transient failures during signup-related operations.

## User Experience Flow
1. User lands on Signup Page from Landing Page or navigation.
2. User enters required fields: Email, Name, Password; optional Company.
3. User reviews terms and privacy policy; checks acceptance.
4. User opts into social signup (Google or GitHub) if desired.
5. Optional quick onboarding panel appears (or can be toggled) to select modules: Projects, Content, Finance, Health; review onboarding preview.
6. User clicks primary CTA (Create account / Start onboarding).
7. Frontend validates input; submits to /auth/signup or /auth/oauth/signup accordingly.
8. Backend creates user, initiates email verification if needed, and creates session.
9. If onboarding is opted-in, redirect to Onboarding / Setup Wizard; otherwise navigate to Dashboard with an immediate first login tour.
10. If email verification is required, present instructions and a verification prompt or route to Email Verification Page.
11. On success, show a confirmation toast and guide user to subsequent steps.

Edge cases and alternate flows:
- If email already exists: show a clear message with login options and password reset link.
- If social signup fails: provide fallback to email/password registration with helpful guidance.
- If verification email fails to send: offer retry and show status messaging.
- If user selects modules that require integrations: show a friendly explanation and proceed to onboarding post-signup.
- 2FA readiness hint: suggest enabling 2FA after sign-in; do not block signup for 2FA at this stage unless policy requires.

## Technical Specifications

Data Models: (Schema details)
- User
  - id: string (UUID)
  - email: string
  - name: string
  - company?: string
  - passwordHash?: string
  - createdAt: Date
  - isEmailVerified: boolean
  - twoFactorEnabled?: boolean
  - preferredModules: string[] // e.g., ["Projects","Content","Finance","Health"]
  - onboardingState: {
      stage: 'not_started'|'modules_selected'|'integrations_connected'|'data_imported'|'cronjob_created'|...,
      modulesSelected?: string[],
      integrationsConnected?: string[],
      lastUpdated?: Date
    }
  - roles?: string[]
- Session
  - id: string
  - userId: string
  - createdAt: Date
  - expiresAt: Date
  - deviceInfo?: string
  - ipAddress?: string
- VerificationToken
  - id: string
  - userId: string
  - token: string
  - expiresAt: Date
  - type: 'email_verification'
- OnboardingProgress
  - id: string
  - userId: string
  - modulesSelected: string[]
  - integrationsConnected: string[]
  - dataImported?: boolean
  - cronjobCreated?: boolean
  - lastUpdated: Date

API Endpoints: (Routes and methods)
- POST /auth/signup
  - Body: { email, name, password, company?, modules?: string[], agreeToTerms: boolean, onboardingPreferred?: boolean }
  - Response: { userId, sessionId, needsEmailVerification: boolean, onboardingPath?: 'wizard'|'dashboard' }
- POST /auth/oauth/signup
  - Body: { provider: 'google'|'github', oauthToken: string, onboardingPreferred?: boolean }
  - Response: { userId, sessionId, needsEmailVerification: boolean, onboardingPath?: 'wizard'|'dashboard' }
- POST /auth/verify-email
  - Body: { token: string }
  - Response: { success: boolean, userId?: string, onboardingPath?: 'wizard'|'dashboard' }
- GET /modules/availability
  - Response: { availableModules: string[] }

Security: 
- Enforce TLS, CSRF safety on forms.
- Server-side validation and sanitization for all inputs.
- Ensure no sensitive data is exposed in responses (password hashes, tokens).
- Use httpOnly secure cookies for session tokens.
- Implement proper rate limiting and account lockout policies where appropriate.
- Ensure proper authorization on onboarding endpoints (only authenticated users can proceed).

Validation:
- Frontend:
  - Email must be valid format.
  - Password strength must meet minimum requirements (e.g., min length, variety).
  - Name must be present; Company optional.
  - Terms checkbox must be checked.
- Backend:
  - Validate email format and uniqueness.
  - Validate password with strength policy.
  - Validate module selections against allowed list.
  - Validate onboardingPreferred flag and ensure user is allowed to proceed.

